of cells."},{"label":"C","text":"phagocytosis of apoptotic cells by surrounding healthy cells."},{"label":"D","text":"release of free radicals."},{"label":"E","text":"localised oedema. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Cellular injury and adaptation SUBCATEGORY --- FILE NUMBER SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 18 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 CORRECT RESPONSE C APPLICATION"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"30d21fe6748f83cf633471612012329fb2d7847b"},{"id":"q-cb9afdc7f2c8","stem":"A substance that is not known to accumulate intracellularly is ??.??.??","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"melanin."},{"label":"B","text":"haemosiderin."},{"label":"C","text":"tattoo ink."},{"label":"D","text":"pus."},{"label":"E","text":"lipofuscin. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Cellular injury and adaptation SUBCATEGORY --- FILE NUMBER SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 28 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 CORRECT RESPONSE D APPLICATION"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"