rmally found in an atheromatous plaque include all the following, except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"smooth muscle cells."},{"label":"B","text":"foam cells."},{"label":"C","text":"macrophages."},{"label":"D","text":"lymphocytes."},{"label":"E","text":"platelets. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Cardiovascular system SUBCATEGORY Atherosclerosis FILE NUMBER"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8552d3ea9d2b46ec37ec03f2661d83ac47c97134"},{"id":"q-a8ce0db386e4","stem":"Raynaud disease characteristically: ??.??.??","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"occurs almost entirely in young male cigarette smokers."},{"label":"B","text":"is associated with atherosclerosis."},{"label":"C","text":"occurs primarily in tropical climates."},{"label":"D","text":"is the result of a vasospastic reaction."},{"label":"E","text":"involves elastic arteries. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY SUBCATEGORY FILE NUMBER SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 499 ORIGINATOR ECFMG sample questions DATE 1990 CORRECT RESPONSE D APPLICATION"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassi