n produce cirrhosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Hepatitis B is NOT present in stool"},{"label":"C","text":"HBeAb confers immunity against Hepatitis B"},{"label":"D","text":"Hepatitis C is commonly sexually transmitted"},{"label":"E","text":"Hepatitis D increases the risk of hepatocellular carcinoma in people with hepatitis B infection SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Liver and biliary tract SUBCATEGORY Hepatitis FILE NUMBER SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 844 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 CORRECT RESPONSE B APPLICATION"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Virology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"583da6e11fea70e7e4a1c55d66da621a34c9b87e"},{"id":"q-402979b8e816","stem":"The pathogenesis of cirrhosis involves all of the following EXCEPT: ??.??.??","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","topicOriginal":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","subtopic":"Cirrhosis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"demolition of collagen in the space of Disse"},{"label":"B","text":"chronic inflammation"},{"label":"C","text":"conversion of Kupffer cells into fibroblast-like cells"},{"label":"D","text":"loss of fenestrations in sinusoidal capillaries"},{"label":"E","text":"disruption of normal hepatic blood flow SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Liver and biliary tract SUBCATEGORY Cirrhosis FILE NUMBER SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 834-835 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 CORRECT RESPONSE A APPLICATION 12a Gastrointestinal tract"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasS