utol .........T...... visual disturbances: initially red/green color blindness .........T...... Color vision should be monitored during prolonged treatment. .........F...... unwanted side effect gout, which is associated with high concentrations of plasma urates .........F...... cause haemolytic anaemia in individuals with glucose-6-phosphate deficiency .........F...... decreases the metabolism of the antiepileptic agents, phenytoin, and carbamazepine","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Neurology","topicOriginal":"Neurology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Neurology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b96cdc8de3bb","stem":"Angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitor .........T......reduce preload .........F......is positive inotrope .........F......do not cause cough .........F......no effect on after load ............F...causes muscles fasiculation 23 Which of the following induces microsomal enzymes ......T.........Phenobarbitone ......T.........Ethanol ......T.........Diazepam .........F......Ketaconazole .........T......Nevirapine","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-7b3579bf3079","stem":"Tolerance and physio