ocks L-type calcium channels"},{"label":"B","text":"It increases heart rate"},{"label":"C","text":"It relaxes coronary artery smooth muscle"},{"label":"D","text":"It depresses cardiac contractility"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9926ac02b419","stem":"All of the following calcium channel blockers are useful in the treatment of cardiac arrhythmias EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bepridil"},{"label":"B","text":"Diltiazem"},{"label":"C","text":"Verapamil"},{"label":"D","text":"Nifedipine"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3af0915ee8ea","stem":"All of the following are common adverse effects of calcium channel blockers EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Skeletal muscle weakness"},{"label":"B","text":"Dizziness"},{"label":"C","text":"Headache"},{"label":"D","text":"Flushing"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicat