s strongly to an α2-globulin and albumin with lower affinity"},{"label":"B","text":"Estradiol is converted by liver and other tissues to estron and estriol and their 2-hydroxylated derivatives and conjugated metabolites and excreted in the bile"},{"label":"C","text":"Estrone and estriol have lower affinity for the estrogen receptors than estradiol"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1a71d28c2c21124372d1088e02b9e7cdd9ec1ef3"},{"id":"q-2de183c84ac1","stem":"Indications of synthetic estrogens are following, EXCEPT: 94","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Primary hypogonadism"},{"label":"B","text":"Postmenopausal hormonal therapy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hormonal contraception"},{"label":"D","text":"For treatment of simple obesity"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2d95bae95680","stem":"Main complications of estrogens’ therapy include the following","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Postmenopausal uterine bleeding"},{"label":"B","text":"Breast tenderness"},{"label