calcium)"},{"label":"C","text":"Calcium phosphate (25% calcium)"},{"label":"D","text":"Calcium citrate (17% calcium)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-28d8f00ea812","stem":"Correct statements about magnesium include all of the following, EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Magnesium is mainly an intracellular cation, and is the fourth most abundant cation in the body"},{"label":"B","text":"The recommended dietary amounts of magnesium have been set at 6 mg/kg day (350-400 mg)"},{"label":"C","text":"The most common specific causes encountered in clinical practice are: diet, alcoholism (drinking), diarrhea and malabsorption, diabetes mellitus, diuretics, and drugs such as aminoglycosides and amphotericin"},{"label":"D","text":"It is a physiological calcium agonist"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b3da950f1bf5","stem":"Which of the magnesium preparation is the most preferable for I.V. injection","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Magnesium sulfate"},{"label":"B","text":"Magnesium chloride"},{"label":"C","text":"Magnesium glutamate"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-17354e8c785a","stem":"Which of the oral magnesium preparations is often the preparation of choice","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Magnesium lactate"},{"label":"B","text":"Magnesium oxide"},{"label":"C","text":"MagneB6 (Mg pidolate / Mg lactate + pyridoxine hydrochloride)"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2f875591fac7","stem":"Correct statements about fluoride include all of the following, EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fluoride is effective for the prophylaxis of dental caries"},{"label":"B","text":"Fluoride is accumulated by bone and teeth, where it may stabilize the hydroxyapatite crystal 120"},{"label":"C","text":"Subjects living in areas with naturally fluoridated water (1-2 ppm) had more dental caries and fewer vertebral compression fractures than subjects living in nonfluoridated water areas"},{"label":"D","text":"Chronic exposure to very high level of fluoride dust in the inspired air results in crippling fluorosis, characterized by thickening of the cortex of long bones and bony exostoses."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d189984bce5d","stem":"Which of the following statements refers to gallium nitrate","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is approved by the FDA for the management of hypercalcemia of malignancy"},{"label":"B","text":"This drug acts by inhibiting bone resorption"},{"label":"C","text":"Because of potential nephrotoxicity, patients should be well-hydrated and have good renal output before starting the infusion"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-917b423f7f19","stem":"Which of the following statements refers to plicamycin (formerly mithramycin)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Duration of action is usually several days"},{"label":"B","text":"Mechanism of cytotoxic action appears to involve its binding to DNA, possibly through an antibiotic-Mg2+ complex."},{"label":"C","text":"The drug causes plasma calcium levels to decrease, apparently through an action on osteoclasts that is independent of its action on tumor cells and useful in hypercalcemia."},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d6bc7e4d0cdf","stem":"Unwanted effects of plicamycin (formerly mithramycin) are the following, EXEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Thrombocytopenia"},{"label":"B","text":"GI toxicity"},{"label":"C","text":"Bleeding disorders"},{"label":"D","text":"Fractures"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f67862e9ba92","stem":"Which of the following synthetic steroids shows predominantly mineralocorticoid action?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hydrocortisone"},{"label":"B","text":"Spironolactone"},{"label":"C","text":"Dexamethasone"},{"label":"D","text":"Fludrocortisone"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditF