 than HIT2 ......T.........may accumulate in patients with renal impairment ......F.........must be administered by a physician in a hospital ......F.........do need patient’s agreement in case of infectious diseases ......T.........are required for drug approval","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-84cb626ee03d","stem":"Heparin ......T.........is usually given to every immobilized patient ......F.........treatment length is restricted to 9 days ......T.........its complication HIT1 is less dangerous than HIT2 ......T.........may accumulate in patients with renal impairment ......F.........must be administered by a physician in a hospital","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-2101c23873c7","stem":"Clinical studies Clinical studies ......F.........always contain a placebo group ......F.........must be financed by the manufacturer of the investigated drug ......T.........contain defined patient inclusion criteria ......F.........do need patient’s agreement in case of infectious diseases .....