ulates appetite and often cause weight gain G. reduce gluconeogenesis in the liver H. serious side effect is lactic acidosis I. Is a biguanides and does not affect the output of insulin J. effective in Type 1diabetes mellitus patients in concert with insulin","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-984e173557ba","stem":"Pancreatic islets F. Alpha cells (A cells) secrete the hormone insulin. G. Beta cells (B cells) produce glucagons and are the most abundant of the islet cells. H. Delta cells (D cells) secrete the hormone insulin I. Somatostatin is synthesized and secreted from alpha cells J. glucagon has the effect of increasing blood glucose levels","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-43a499ac829d","stem":"Which of the following side effects is atypical for metformin? F. Nausea G. Vomiting H. Metallic tatse I. hypoglycaemia J. lactate acidosis","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Endocrinology","topicOriginal":"Endocrinology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSource