armacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is a reversible cyclo-oxygenase inhibitor"},{"label":"B","text":"Has analgesic and antipyretic properties"},{"label":"C","text":"Has anti-inflammatory properties"},{"label":"D","text":"Can cause renal impairment"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9444c720e6ae","stem":"Which of the following is the longest acting benzodiazepine? ............... Alprazolam ............... flurazepam ............... Flumazenil ............... Midazolam ............... Triazolam","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"CNS Pharmacology · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"CNS Pharmacology","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"CNS Pharmacology · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-8d44cfa3ab2d","stem":"Glyceryltrinitrate –Nitroglycerin ............... relaxes resistance vessels of the arterial circulation ............... decreases after load on the heart and thus decrease oxygen demands of the heart ............... Nitroglycerin ointment can relief angina and prolong exercise capacity ............... increase intracellular cGMP which in turn reduces intracellular calcium ............... used for treatment of peripheral vascular disease","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-dedac5b3ef5e","stem":"The mechanism of action of theophylline includes; ...............beta adrenoceptor agonist ...............inhibition of phosphodiesterase ...............direct action of intracellular calcium concentration ...............antagonism of adenosine receptors ...............muscarinic receptor antagonist 13Which of the following groups of drugs should be considered in the treatment of acute asthma ...............beta adrenergic agonists ...............beta adrenergic antagonists ...............anticholinergics ...............glucocorticoids ...............cromolyn sodium","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-fc32cf327564","stem":"Receptors at the sites mentioned are muscarinic ...............sweat galnds ...............smooth muscles of the respiratory tract ...............adrenal medulla ...............salivary gland ...............circular muscle of the iris 15The toxicity of MAO inhibitors that is related to dietary constituents is due 