ebiasis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chloroquine."},{"label":"B","text":"Emetine. T © Diloxinide."},{"label":"D","text":"Metronidazole."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f2ae25d0832d","stem":"The following drugs are used in the treatment of hepatic amoebiasis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chloroquine."},{"label":"B","text":"Emetine. T © Metronidazole."},{"label":"D","text":"Tetracycline."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8a2c6d1d5f0b","stem":"Which of the following drugs act by nucleophilic attack on nitrogen 7 of guanine to disrupt the base pairing patterns.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cyclophosphamide."},{"label":"B","text":"Fluorouracil. F © Methotrexate."},{"label":"D","text":"Prednisolone."},{"label":"E","text":"thioguanine."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6c95077b1bdc","stem":"The following are amino acids neurotransmitters which decrease neural activity.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Neurology","topicOriginal":"Neurology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Glycine."},{"label":"B","text":"Glutamic acid. T © GABA."},{"label":"D","text":"Leucin enkephalin."},{"label":"E","text":"Tyrosine."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Neurology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bc61a3c20b52","stem":"The following mechanisms may explain the phenomenon underlying desensitization and tachyphylaxis to drugs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Loss of receptors T"},{"label":"B","text":"Exhaustion of mediators T"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased metabolic degradation T"},{"label":"D","text":"Physiological adaptation T"},{"label":"E","text":"Change in receptor configuration T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ad6af4346241","stem":"The following ions are essential in excitations of neurons or any other excitable tissue","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Neurology","topicOriginal":"Neurology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"K+ F"},{"label":"B","text":"Na+ T"},{"label":"C","text":"Ca+ T"},{"label":"D","text":"CL-F"},{"label":"E","text":"Magnesium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Neurology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-00e4dc9344fb","stem":"Side effects of insulin G. True.........Hypoglycemia H. False.........Weight loss I. True.........Lipodystrophy J. False.........Angioedema K. False.........Retinopathy L. False.........proton pump inhibitor M. False............H2-receptor antagonist N. False......Gastrin inhibitor O. False............Muscarinic receptor antagonist P. False............H1 receptor antagonist","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Endocrinology","topicOriginal":"Endocrinology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Endocrinology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-d415e5641d98","stem":"Acid suppressing agents Q. True......... Antiacids R. True............ H2 receptor antagonists S. True...............muscarinic receptor blockers T. True...............adenylate cyclase inhibitors U. False...............potassium pump inhibitors","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Autonomic Pharmacology · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Autonomic Pharmacology","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Autonomic Pharmacology · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c2c895e49987","stem":"Misoprostol V. True...............synthetic prostaglandin E, analogue W. True............increase production of gastric mucus X. True...............increase production of bicarbonate Y. True...............contraindicated in pregnancy Z. False...............chelating agent","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-9c47ab56884f","stem":"Osmotic laxative ...True............Magnesium sulphate ...True............sodium sulphate ...True............sodium potassium tartate ...False............Sodium bicarbonate ...False............aluminium hydroxide","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-fb8a5826e79f","stem":"Metformin True...............may cause lactic acidosis False...............Is useful in alcoholic diabetic patient False...............Causes hypoglycemia in non diabetic patient False...............Is used in gestational diabetes False............Improves appetite and patients gain weight","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Endocrinology","topicOriginal":"Endocrinology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Endocrinology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-6a3d3cf84444","stem":"Heparin ......T.........is usually given to every immobilized patient ......F.........treatment length is restricted to 9 days ......T.........its complication HIT1 is less dangerous than HIT2 ......T.........may accumulate in patients with renal impairment ......F.........must be administered by a physician in a hospital ......F.........does need patient’s agreement in case of infectious diseases ......T.........is required for drug approval","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-72c10598db63","stem":"Clinical studies Clinical studies ......F.........always contain a placebo group ......F.........must be financed by the manufacturer of the investigated drug ......T.........contain defined patient inclusion criteria ......F.........does not need patient’s agreement in case of infectious diseases ......T.........is required for drug approval","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-2e5c212ffe09","stem":"Which of the following side effects is atypical for glitazones? F. Arrhythmias G. Edema H. Heart failure I. Myocardial infarction(advantageous of glitazone also protect stroke) J. Bone fractures","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-40eecd1d148c","stem":"Which of the following antidiabetic drugs should not be used as a monotherapy of DM2? F. Insulin G. Metformin H. Repaglinide I. Nateglinide J. Glibenclamide","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Endocrinology","topicOriginal":"Endocrinology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Endocrinology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-34a1b5af530d","stem":"Which of the following drugs should be primarily applied in the prophylaxis of peri-operative thrombosis? K. Aspirin L. Warfarin M. Heparin N. Clopidogrel O. Streptokinase SECTION III: MATCHING ITEMS Match the members of group A to those of group B by choosing and writing (in the space provided). The letter of the most corresponding member of group B. Members of group B shall be used only once and some neither shall nor be used at all. GROUP A","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8623a4a8c020","stem":"Regional considerations Core emergency sequence Resuscitate → risk-stratify → identify variceal vs non-variceal → endoscopy → definitive hemostasis → prevent recurrence. Do not let endoscopy distract from physiology: an unstable patient needs airway/circulatory stabilization first. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-32140da7f6ac","stem":"Clinical presentation Hematemesis may be fresh red blood/clots. Coffee-ground emesis suggests acid-altered blood. Melena is black tarry stool. Brisk massive UGIB may cause hematochezia. Severity clues include syncope, tachycardia, hypotension, oliguria, cool peripheries and altered mental status. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-48d127c2bc17","stem":"Examination ABC assessment first. Record pulse, BP, RR, SpO2, capillary refill, mental status and urine output. Look for jaundice, spider nevi, palmar erythema, ascites, splenomegaly and encephalopathy. Abdominal and rectal examination help identify tenderness, masses, melena or hematochezia. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-57575ff4747c","stem":"Immediate resuscitation Airway protection if massive ongoing hematemesis, severe encephalopathy or inability to protect airway. Give oxygen for hypoxemia. Insert two large-bore IV cannulas; send FBC, U&E/creatinine, LFT/albumin, coagulation profile, lactate and group/crossmatch. Treat significant hypotension with crystalloid while arranging blood products. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-97697af9a015","stem":"Laboratory interpretation Hb trend is more useful than one early value. Urea can rise disproportionately from digestion/absorption of blood protein and hypovolemia. Platelets, INR, renal function, albumin and lactate help define comorbidity and physiologic severity. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a7024715dde6","stem":"Transfusion For most hemodynamically stable patients without major cardiovascular disease, a restrictive RBC strategy uses a threshold near Hb 7 g/dL and target roughly 7–9 g/dL. Significant cardiovascular disease may justify a higher threshold. Avoid unnecessary over-transfusion in portal-hypertensive bleeding. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a4ae8d840c4d","stem":"Glasgow-Blatchford Score Pre-endoscopy score using urea, hemoglobin, systolic BP, pulse, melena, syncope, hepatic disease and cardiac failure. GBS 0–1 identifies very-low-risk patients who may be managed as outpatients when clinically appropriate. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3b303b557525","stem":"H. pylori Test peptic-ulcer bleeding patients for H. pylori and eradicate if positive. Acute bleeding and PPI therapy can reduce test sensitivity, so repeat testing when appropriate and confirm eradication after treatment. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6ca9212af0dd","stem":"Recurrent peptic ulcer bleed Re-resuscitate and repeat therapeutic endoscopy. If repeat endoscopic hemostasis fails, proceed to transcatheter arterial embolization where available. Surgery is required if embolization is unavailable or unsuccessful. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-594e688cf282","stem":"ABC/resuscitation and restrictive transfusion. 2) Start vasoactive drug immediately. 3) Give prophylactic antibiotic. 4) Endoscopy within 12 h after resuscitation. 5) Esophageal varix → band ligation. 6) Assess early for pre-emptive TIPS. 7) Persistent bleeding → bridge therapy if needed and rescue TIPS. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b95b09c3640e","stem":"Vasoactive drugs Octreotide: 50 microgram IV bolus then 50 microgram/hour infusion. Terlipressin: commonly 2 mg IV every 4 hours initially, then de-escalated per response/protocol. Somatostatin is another option. Start at presentation when variceal bleeding is suspected and continue up to about 5 days. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c89a62e9716a","stem":"Pre-emptive & rescue TIPS High-risk patients should be considered for pre-emptive TIPS within 72 h, preferably within 24 h. Important groups include Child-Pugh C ≤13 and selected Child-Pugh B patients with active bleeding at endoscopy. Persistent bleeding despite drug + endoscopic therapy requires rescue TIPS where available. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b7596fabaae2","stem":"Balloon tamponade Sengstaken–Blakemore/Minnesota balloon tamponade can temporarily control uncontrolled esophageal variceal bleeding but risks aspiration, ulceration, necrosis and perforation. It is a bridge to definitive therapy, not definitive management. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-131136bab147","stem":"Mallory–Weiss & Dieulafoy Mallory–Weiss: longitudinal mucosal tear after forceful retching; most stop spontaneously, ongoing bleeding can be treated endoscopically. Dieulafoy: large submucosal artery through a tiny defect causing dramatic intermittent bleeding; mechanical/combination endoscopic therapy is preferred. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-56c91cb2df2d","stem":"Antithrombotics Balance hemorrhage against thrombosis. Withhold anticoagulants in major bleeding and use reversal for severe/life-threatening bleeding as appropriate. Aspirin for secondary cardiovascular prevention is generally continued or restarted early after hemostasis. Resume anticoagulation after bleeding control according to thrombotic risk, often within or soon after about 7 days in non-variceal bleeding when appropriate. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-38eeb21db518","stem":"Discharge & prevention Document source and hemostasis; eradicate H. pylori; avoid unnecessary NSAIDs; optimize gastroprotection; restart antithrombotics safely; correct iron deficiency; for varices arrange NSBB + serial EBL and hepatology follow-up. Upper GI Bleeding · Master Level","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7dd2ab8d7fdb","stem":"Regional considerations In East African practice, consider chronic HBV/HCV, alcohol-related disease and schistosomiasis as causes of portal hypertension and varices. Schistosomiasis can cause presinusoidal portal hypertension with relatively preserved hepatocellular synthetic function. Resource-sensitive care depends on rapid resuscitation, early vasoactive drug/antibiotic treatment when varices are suspected, therapeutic endoscopy and clear referral pathways.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-792262fd62be","stem":"Angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitor ......... ......reduce preload ......... ......is positive inotrope ......... ......do not cause cough ......... ......no effect on after load ............ ...causes muscles fasiculation 23 Which of the following induces microsomal enzymes ...... .........Phenobarbitone ...... .........Ethanol ...... .........Diazepam ......... ......Ketaconazole ......... ......Nevirapine","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-3fb54b12be7d","stem":"The following can be correctly described as drug receptors","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ion channels F"},{"label":"B","text":"G-protein coupled receptors T"},{"label":"C","text":"Enzymes F"},{"label":"D","text":"Carrier molecules F"},{"label":"E","text":"The cell nucleus F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"90a22b0a6f085c12239f4f2183be1aa7be7462c5"},{"id":"q-e0677c065dbb","stem":"The following side effects of Tricyclic antidepressants are correctly matched with the receptor involved","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Weight gain-H2 blockade. -F"},{"label":"B","text":"Constipation-M1 blockade -.T"},{"label":"C","text":".Decreased blood pressure-β blockade. -F"},{"label":"D","text":"Increased blood pressure-α (alpha) blockade. -T"},{"label":"E","text":"Weight gain-H1 blockade. -T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"462ba247f8bda14fec7033eb0b8c6336fe27f263"},{"id":"q-9c0b6b9062e8","stem":"Current therapies for parkinsonism include the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dopa-decarboxylase inhibitors - F"},{"label":"B","text":"Dopamine antagonists - T"},{"label":"C","text":"MAO-A inhibitors - T"},{"label":"D","text":"Amantadine - F it increase dopamine release it is antipakinsonism, antiviral, and PCP."},{"label":"E","text":"Nor epinephrine antagonists - F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"060ad3694939d2db75762a9a6cac3b0e6dd4d951"},{"id":"q-8ab24c47196a","stem":"Epinephrine increases BP by which of the following mechanisms","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Baroreceptor reflex- T"},{"label":"B","text":"Myocardial stimulation - T"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased heart rate - T"},{"label":"D","text":"Vasoconstriction of skeletal muscles - F"},{"label":"E","text":"Vasodilatation in skin and mucosa - F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8cbd55c4b3d0fa20d3308f80a4f4798d65e045d0"},{"id":"q-98eaa0d24893","stem":"The following have both alpha and beta blocking effects","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cavedilol - T"},{"label":"B","text":"Atenelo l - F"},{"label":"C","text":"Propranolol - F"},{"label":"D","text":"Proctolo -l F"},{"label":"E","text":"Alprenolol - F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"532c25f9457e3d9f7e5cc2a34f6073c224ab5ab1"},{"id":"q-90e6b7a5a2db","stem":"The following statements about nitrates are true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are rapidly metabolized in the liver. T"},{"label":"B","text":"They inhibit guanyl cyclase enzyme. F"},{"label":"C","text":"They are associated with tolerance especially when higher doses are used. T"},{"label":"D","text":"They decrease preload. T"},{"label":"E","text":"They can be co-adminstered concurrently with sidenafil. F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e7ec36b04a75f06a3a17a0ec802f00ad929e91ed"},{"id":"q-e1e286130ba3","stem":"The following are side effects of nitrates EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Postural hypontesion. F"},{"label":"B","text":"Tachycardia F"},{"label":"C","text":"Throbbing headache F"},{"label":"D","text":"Methaemoglobinemia which is seen with nitrites F"},{"label":"E","text":"Bradycardia T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"9bc1449680e06bb5dadc28b58d3165aa49dd8cb7"},{"id":"q-cc8e758dee60","stem":"2.4 Neonate septicemia Neonatal Sepsis affects only neonates, thus from the data collected in 2009 from Muhimbili National Hospital in the neonatal ward, shows that 330 neonates were 9 admitted whereas, from the data collected at SFRH, Ifakara in 2016 shows that there has been an admission of 37 neonates, 15 of them being males and 22 females. This shows how seriously neonatal sepsis affects neonates in Tanzania.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1633669f01e0","stem":"3.1. Mild Anemia Mild anemia is the worldwide disease affecting most low income countries such as Tanzania leading to maternal death and adverse pregnancy outcome despite of 11 achievement of maternal and child health related programs, it is still a problem in Ifakara where 37children were admitted, 22 of them being male children and 15 being female children at SFRH in December 2016.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8ea7e6785754","stem":"6.1. Nephrotic syndrome Nephrotic syndrome can affect any age, although it is mainly found in adults with a ratio of adults to children of 26 to 1. This is the reason that only who were above sixty (5patients) found to be recorded at SFRH data in 2016. There are also differences in epidemiology between the sexes, the disease is more common in men than in women by a ratio of 2 to 1. The data from SFRH shows the ratio of 5 to 0.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-61c377e70dc1","stem":"The following is a risk factor for endometrial carcinoma. Prolonged unopposed oestrogen, High parity, Turner’s syndrome Late menarche and early menopause Use of progesterone contained contraceptives","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b16400346d0a","stem":"The following is delivery consideration for a pregnant woman with fibroid; Vaginal delivery is relatively contraindicated, Caesarean myomectomy if abdominal delivery is indicated to prevent postpartum haemorrhage, Better avoid caesarean myomectomy even if abdominal delivery is indicated, Assist second stage of labour, Augment labour as fibroid commonly causes poor uterine contractions","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3cf74b8e2b53","stem":"The following are common complications of fibroids in pregnancy except:- Dystocia Premature labour Malposition Postpartum hemorrhage Precipitated labour","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b132077623f6","stem":"Antiretroviral therapy is recommended for all HIV positive: Women regardless of CD4 count or WHO clinical stage Breastfeeding women when CD4 count is ≤ 200copies/μl Pregnant and breastfeeding women when CD4 count is ≤ 350copies/μl Pregnant women as soon as they are diagnosed regardless of the CD4 count. Pregnant women on ART to switch their ART regiment to didanosine + stavudine + efavirenz.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-433f3816d024","stem":"Regarding prevention of mother to child transmission of HIV: Combined antiretroviral prophylaxis is recommended for all pregnant women or breastfeeding women with HIV. Antiretroviral therapy should be stopped after stopping breastfeeding when CD4 count is ≥350 copies/μl ART is recommended for pregnant and breastfeeding women when CD4 count is ≤ 350copies/μl otherwise use PMTCT prophylactic regimen. ART should continue throughout pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding and for life. All infants born to HIV positive women should receive ARV prophylaxis from birth to 2 weeks of age.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-82ea36660da9","stem":"The following micronutrient prevents development of neural tube defects and reduces risk of some other birth defects Zinc Folic acid Iron Iodine Vitamin A","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fbbe462b4812","stem":"What is the mechanism of action of oral contraceptives? Direct suppressive effects on the follicles in the ovaries Suppression of gonadotropin-releasing factors leading anovulation Positive feedback mechanism to the pituitary gland and hypothalamus Suppression of the hypothalamus and higher centres in the brain","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b3b93496567f","stem":"The following are estrogen preparations commonly used in monophasic combined oral contraceptives Ethinyloestradiol and levonorgestrel Noresthisterone and levonorgestrel Ethinyloestradiol and mestranol Estrone and mestranol Ethinyloestradiol and gestrone","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bdb087818166","stem":"The following are causes of primary amenorrhoea _______ Menopause _______ Sheehan’s syndrome _______ Premature ovarian failure _______ Transverse vaginal septum _______ Agenesis of the ovaries","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cd7aa9316cd6","stem":"The following are recommended PMTCT interventions in HIV positive women _______ Active management of 3rd stage of labour to avoid postpartum haemorrhage _______ Rupture of membranes to shortage time of labour _______ Immediate suction of the newborn to remove maternal genital secretions _______ Perform episiotomy to facilitate second stage of labour _______ Augmentation of labour to reduce transmission of HIV to the baby Uterine fibroids are: _______ The most common malignant tumours found in women. _______ More common in the black than Caucasian population. _______ Encapsulated tumours. _______ Fibrous tissues in origin _______ Associated with sarcomatous change in almost 10% of cases.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e8b98986a85d","stem":"Write your examination number on each sheet of paper you use","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1aa012f42d39","stem":"This paper consists of four sections. SECTION A: MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS (30 MARKS) Instructions: Circle the most correct answer. No penalty for incorrect response. One mark will be awarded for each correct response","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["answer_explanation_mixed_into_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7f5c18ed6b39","stem":"MS GK was 18 years presented with primary amenorrhea, intermittent abdominal pain, difficult micturition and a lower abdominal swelling for 2 years. The site of pathology is most likely in the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vagina"},{"label":"B","text":"Uterus,"},{"label":"C","text":"Ovaries,"},{"label":"D","text":"Anterior pituitary gland"},{"label":"E","text":"Hypothalamus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-538b92576563","stem":"What is mostly likely diagnosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dysfunctional uterine bleeding"},{"label":"B","text":"Endometrial cancer"},{"label":"C","text":"Cervical cancer"},{"label":"D","text":"a, b, and c"},{"label":"E","text":"Ovarian cancer"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-527a15bf230d","stem":"What test or procedure can you do to confirm your diagnosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pelvic ultrasound"},{"label":"B","text":"Fractional curettage"},{"label":"C","text":"Wedge biopsy"},{"label":"D","text":"Speculum exam"},{"label":"E","text":"Punch biopsy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4409bbf39f74","stem":"The most common type of breech presents with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Flexion of both the thighs and legs at the knees"},{"label":"B","text":"Flexed thigh on the abdomen and legs extended at the knees"},{"label":"C","text":"Footling with only one leg"},{"label":"D","text":"Footling with both two legs"},{"label":"E","text":"Compound presentation Mrs. Hamisi 48 year old woman presented with contact vaginal bleeding and copious offensive vaginal discharge. A tumor mass arising from the cervix involving the parametrium was noted. Ultrasound revealed bilateral hydronephrosis. Use this information to answer question 6, 7and 8"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3e08ff8730ab","stem":"The following are predisposing risk factor to this condition EXCEPT?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Candidacies"},{"label":"B","text":"Human Papilloma virus Type 16& 18"},{"label":"C","text":"Multiparity"},{"label":"D","text":"Early sexual intercourse < 15 years"},{"label":"E","text":"Combine oral contraceptive"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-66c0daf32ba3","stem":"What is the clinical stage of this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Stage IB"},{"label":"B","text":"Stage IIA"},{"label":"C","text":"Stage IVA"},{"label":"D","text":"Stage IIIA"},{"label":"E","text":"Stage IIIB"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f13fff781177","stem":"What mode of treatment would you mostly recommend for this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hysterectomy"},{"label":"B","text":"Conization"},{"label":"C","text":"Radiotherapy"},{"label":"D","text":"Chemotherapy"},{"label":"E","text":"Trachelectomy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-698f430e81c5","stem":"A 20 years old girl gave a history of amenorrhea following induced abortion and excessive intrauterine curettage. Her amenorrheoic condition is commonly","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Characterized by normal FSH and LH"},{"label":"B","text":"Caused by HIV endometritis"},{"label":"C","text":"Aggravated by progesterone challenge when trying to establish the diagnosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Anovulatory in nature"},{"label":"E","text":"Associated with abnormal secondary sex characteristics MS AD presented with mild vaginal bleeding, severe abdominal pain, fainting attacks due to hypovolemia and rebound abdominal tenderness in early pregnancy. Use this information to answer question 11and 12"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5b6264dca7b3","stem":"Which of the following is the major risk factor for this condition in Tanzania?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pendaculated fibroids"},{"label":"B","text":"Chromosomal abnormalities"},{"label":"C","text":"Adolescent sexuality leading to intentional termination of pregnancy"},{"label":"D","text":"Pelvic inflammatory disease"},{"label":"E","text":"Congenital anomalies of the internal genital organs"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9ddf9d2b514e","stem":"In addition to resuscitation the ultimate treatment should include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Evacuation"},{"label":"B","text":"Salpinge-oophorectomy"},{"label":"C","text":"Suction curettage"},{"label":"D","text":"Laparotomy"},{"label":"E","text":"Expectant management"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-521e072cc6c9","stem":"What is the next step in the management of this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Perform a vaginal examination every 2 hours until delivery"},{"label":"B","text":"Perform a sterile speculum examination"},{"label":"C","text":"Begin antibiotics"},{"label":"D","text":"Begin oxytocin"},{"label":"E","text":"Expectant management"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2353f94f2242","stem":"What kind of tests can confirm the presence of amniotic fluid?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Keihauer-Betke test"},{"label":"B","text":"Coomb's test"},{"label":"C","text":"Triple screen"},{"label":"D","text":"Ferning test"},{"label":"E","text":"Cough test"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-656fb5c76eef","stem":"The following bacterial infections have been implicated for diagnosis of this patient.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Streptococcus pyogenes and Neisseria gonorrhoae"},{"label":"B","text":"Streptococcus agalactaciae and Streptococcus pyogenes"},{"label":"C","text":"Neisseria gonorrhoae and Listeria monocytogenes"},{"label":"D","text":"Listeria monocytogenes and Salmonella typhi"},{"label":"E","text":"Streptococcus agalactaciae and Neisseria gonorrhoae"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ccda20f73fa7","stem":"After 1 day of expectant management with antibiotics and dexamethasone the patient develops uterine tenderness and fever. What is the next step in management?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Delivery immediately"},{"label":"B","text":"Perform a biophysical profile"},{"label":"C","text":"Change the antibiotics"},{"label":"D","text":"Complete the dose of dexamethasone of 42hours then deliver"},{"label":"E","text":"Continue with expectant management until 34wks"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-202c1f987224","stem":"In cervical cancer screening which set of equipment you basically need for the test?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Theatre lamp,colposcope and acetic acid"},{"label":"B","text":"Theatre lamp,lugos iodine and gynecologist"},{"label":"C","text":"Acetic acid,torch,speculum and examination bed"},{"label":"D","text":"Gynecologist ,colposcope and pathologist"},{"label":"E","text":"Theatre lamp, acetic acid, speculum and examination bed"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b2714af4021b","stem":"The following statements about cancer of the cervix are true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Neoplasia","topicOriginal":"Neoplasia","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Well differentiated squamous cell carcinoma responds well to radiotherapy"},{"label":"B","text":"Poorly differentiated are fast growing tumor and metastasizes earlier"},{"label":"C","text":"Squamous cell carcinoma are the most common of all"},{"label":"D","text":"Adenocarcinoma has worse prognosis than squamous cell carcinoma"},{"label":"E","text":"Adenocarcinoma is derived from the glandular elements of the cervix."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Neoplasia","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1a7d56087a4f","stem":"Ovulation is characterized by the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Regular menstrual periods at monthly intervals"},{"label":"B","text":"Premenstrual molimina"},{"label":"C","text":"Breast tenderness, fluid retention and irritability"},{"label":"D","text":"Functional dysmenorrhea"},{"label":"E","text":"Rising of axillary temperature"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d6105d51c3d1","stem":"The following benign conditions are associated with prolonged menstrual bleeding except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Gynecology","topicOriginal":"Gynecology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Submucus fibroid"},{"label":"B","text":"Endometrial carcinoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Bleeding disorders"},{"label":"D","text":"Adenomyosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Endometrial hyperplasia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Gynecology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7d5b541239bd","stem":"The consumption of DES during pregnancy can cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Uterine didelphysis,uniconuate and bicornuate congenital anomalies"},{"label":"B","text":"Anencephalies"},{"label":"C","text":"Breast abnormalities"},{"label":"D","text":"Cancer of the ovary later in life"},{"label":"E","text":"Vaginal cancer of the female fetus later in life"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4abe37fd6fa8","stem":"The following is usually considered as a grave sign in preeclampsia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blindness"},{"label":"B","text":"Fever above 39°C"},{"label":"C","text":"Severe oedema"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemolysis"},{"label":"E","text":"Severe proteinuria"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5cbcd0ac3275","stem":"The woman complaining of menorrhagia, the following is true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inhibitors of plasminogen activation and fibrinolysis are effective"},{"label":"B","text":"NSAIDS like mefanamic acid can be used"},{"label":"C","text":"Levornegesterol IUCD worsen the menorrhagia"},{"label":"D","text":"Pelvic scan to exclude leiomyoma is advised"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above is true"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e7ab815d15c2","stem":"The most common karyotype among Hydatidform or complete mole?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"46XY"},{"label":"B","text":"47XXY"},{"label":"C","text":"47XYY"},{"label":"D","text":"46XX"},{"label":"E","text":"69XXX"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5dcc1e85356a","stem":"In first trimester abortions, what is the most common chromosomal anomaly?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Autosomal triploidy"},{"label":"B","text":"Autosomal trisomy"},{"label":"C","text":"Sex linked tetraploidy"},{"label":"D","text":"Structural anomaly"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above are true SECTION B: MULTIPLE TRUE / FALSE QUESTIONS (30 MARKS) Instructions: Write the word True for each true statement and the word False for a wrong statement. Half a mark will be awarded to each correct response and the same will be deducted for each incorrect response."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d9c97c5cf0fe","stem":"Primary prevention of cancer of cervix involves the following","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Neoplasia","topicOriginal":"Neoplasia","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"___ Treatment of precancerous lesions before they progress to cervical Cancer"},{"label":"B","text":"___ Health promotion to reduce the risks of HPV infection"},{"label":"C","text":"___ HPV vaccine"},{"label":"D","text":"___ Screening and treatment of cervical intraepithelial neoplasia"},{"label":"E","text":"___ Screening and treatment of Human papilloma virus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Neoplasia","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cd325e8bd7d2","stem":"Which of the following conditions tend to be more common in prime adolescent pregnancies?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"______ Obstructed labour and eclampsia,"},{"label":"B","text":"______ Precipitated labour and placenta praevia,"},{"label":"C","text":"______ Babies with Down’s syndrome and other chromosomal disorders,"},{"label":"D","text":"______ Complications of abortion and malaria,"},{"label":"E","text":"______ Anaemia and malaria."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-31c2f5258e71","stem":"The following liver function changes occur in pregnancy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"____Serum alkaline phosphates rises"},{"label":"B","text":"____Serum cholesterol concentration falls"},{"label":"C","text":"____Serum albumin concentration is reduced"},{"label":"D","text":"____Serum globulin rises"},{"label":"E","text":"____Transaminases concentration falls"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e20e705352e7","stem":"The following feature(s) suggest a diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"___ Amenorrhea of fourteen weeks"},{"label":"B","text":"___ Arias stella reaction on endometrial histology"},{"label":"C","text":"___ Normal sized uterus"},{"label":"D","text":"___ Heavy vaginal bleeding"},{"label":"E","text":"___ Decidual tissue at curettage"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1161db2a37fe","stem":"Fill in the blank space in column A the letter from column B that best corresponds to the clinical features of the syndrome in column A which are. One option can be used only once. Column A Column B i. __Kallmann’s syndrome A. Sexual infantilism and streaked gonads ii. __McCune-Albright syndrome B.Cystic changes in bones iii. __Tunner’s Syndrome C.Retarded bone age iv. __ Silver Syndrome D.Hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism v. __Cushing syndrome E.Hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism F.Heterosexual precocious puberty G.Amenorrheoa and musculinization H. Normal breasts,no sexual hair,uterus&upper vagina","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-18873fe95470","stem":"Mention antimalarial drugs with its route of administration recommended for pregnancy in the current national guidelines for management of malaria. (5 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Uncomplicated malaria in first trimester: _______________"},{"label":"B","text":"Complicated malaria in first trimester: _ ________________"},{"label":"C","text":"Uncomplicated malaria in third trimester: ________________"},{"label":"D","text":"Complicated malaria in third trimester: __________________"},{"label":"E","text":"Intermittent presumptive treatment: ________________"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1d2e0695c435","stem":"List 3 mechanisms does the combined oral contraceptive pill protect against pregnancy and 2 non contraceptive benefit of combined oral contraceptive. (5 marks)","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6560d08c1f6d","stem":"Obstetric fistulae is very stressful condition affecting young girls in developing countries resulting from birth trauma. The injury is complex involving urogenital system; neuromuscular injury and other related structure. Briefly describe the mechanism of the following injuries.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Neurology","topicOriginal":"Neurology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vesicovagina fistula and rectal vaginal fistula. (2 marks)"},{"label":"B","text":"Foot drop(1marks)"},{"label":"C","text":"Amenorrhea(1marks)"},{"label":"D","text":"Perineal dermatitis(1marks) ALL THE BEST"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Neurology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7ef807b3beda","stem":"WHO meningococcal meningitis. https://www.who.int. For Pneumonia.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["url_or_navigation_embedded"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c980c742dd0f","stem":"1. Meningitis Meningitis means inflammation of the meninges. Meninges are the layers covering the surfaces of brain and spinal cord. Meningitis can be transmitted through respiratory fluids also through arthropod borne viruses. Meningitis can be classified into the following types; Fungal meningitis; Bacterial meningitis; Lepto meningitis; Aspectic meningitis; Viral meningitis. Malnutrition; Under five years of age; Overcrowding being risk factors.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9cdf7e0710ee","stem":"2.1. Epidemiology In 2016 pneumonia occurred in approximately 156 million children in the world (151 million in the developing world and 5 million in the developed world). It caused 1.6 million deaths or 28-34% of all deaths to those under five years of age of which 95% occur in the developing world. In Ifakara, Kilombero district, Morogoro Tanzania, data from SFRH in patient diseases department shows that three 3 male and three 3 female children of under one month are affected by pneumonia. This makes a total number of six 6 Children below one month affected by pneumonia in December 2016.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0c0dbadfd9e0","stem":"3. Low Birth Weight This is term used to describe babies born who are born weighting less than 2500gm or 2,5kg , this is mostly caused by premature babies and intrauterine growth restriction where by the baby fail to grow due to problem from mother health ,placental or baby condition.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c09ffe4e57f8","stem":"2.5.1. Epidemiology Globally 23% of neonatal death and 10% of all death in children less than 5 years old , are estimate to occur due to birth asphyxia and account for one million death each year worldwide and according to WHO between four to nine million newborn develop birth asphyxia ,in Ifakara 17 neonate was founded ta have this disease in 2016 Table 3.3: Top five reported disease below one year-2016 NO DISEASES No. of patient by sex Total male female Admission 1 Pneumonia 1 1 2 2 Diarrhea 4 3 7 3 Malaria 7 3 10 4 HIV 10 7 17 5 Anemia 22 15 37 Figure 3.3","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-156dd0278964","stem":"3.1. Mild Anaemia Is a pathological condition arising as a result of low level of hemoglobin in the body. Anaemia can be classified as hemorrhagic ,hemolytic , aplastic, nutritional. Most of children suffer from nutritional anaemia and show symptoms such as dizziness, fatigue, shortness of breath and headache.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1b05d9a991bd","stem":"3.1.1. Epidemiology Mild anaemia is the worldwide disease affect most middle incoming countries such as Tanzania but in developing countries leading to maternal death and adverse pregnancy outcome despite of achievement of maternal and child health related programs its still a problem in Ifakara that show 14 patient where submitted in 2016.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-809072b3f717","stem":"3.2 HIV HIV is human immunodeficiency virus. HIV is virus that attacks the immune system, which is our body’s natural defense against illness. The disease has become the world wide pandemic and becoming most important public health problem at start of the 21 century. The symptoms under one year include swollen abdomen, intermittent, pneumonia.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e944ef485bf9","stem":"5. Abortion Is the ending of pregnancy by removing a foetus or embryo before it can survive by its own. Abortion can be either induced abortion or spontaneous abortion which is miscarriage. Abortion can be caused by cervical incompitance, infection, multiple pregnancy and unintended pregnancy.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f67fb9bf84bd","stem":"5.1. Epidemiology Abortion is performed in whole world, and due to development of science and technology abortion can be done by using mifepristone medicine which was approved in US in 2000 and is used in 31 worldwide countries. In developing country like Tanzania abortion is the main cause of death in women below 60 years due to local method used in abortion. According to statistical data of Ifakara 16 women performed abortion in 2016","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f8a4c6942748","stem":"5.2. Ectopic pregnancy Occur when the fertilized egg attaches itself in a place other than inside the uterus ,it can be cause by infection or inflammation of follopian tube. Mostly of woman who are in high risk of getting ectopic pregnancy are several induced abortion ,smoking and it showing symptoms like abnormal vaginal bleeding, nausea and vomiting.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6ada881bb0c2","stem":"6.1.1. Epidemiology Nephrotic syndrome can affect any age, although it is mainly found in adults with a ratio of adults to children of 26 to 1. This is the reason that only who where above sixty (5patients) found to be recorded in SFRF data in 2016. There are also differences in epidemiology between the sexes, the disease is more common in men than in women by a ratio of 2 to 1. The data from SFRH shows the ratio of 5 to 0. NB: Fractures and Malaria are dealt under 1.5 and 1.2 consecutively","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Epidemiology","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Epidemiology","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4ec52f42e63b","stem":"2.5.1. Epidemiology Globally 23% of neonatal death and 10% of all death in children less than 5 years old , are estimate to occur due to birth asphyxia and account for one million death each year worldwide and according to WHO between four to nine million newborn develop birth asphyxia ,in Ifakara 17 neonate was founded ta have this disease in December 2016. Table 3.3: Top five reported disease below one year-2016 NO DISEASES No. of patient by sex Total male female Admission 1 Pneumonia 1 1 2 2 Diarrhea 4 3 7 3 Malaria 7 3 10 4 HIV 10 7 17 5 Anemia 22 15 37 Figure 3.3","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Respiratory","topicOriginal":"Respiratory","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Respiratory","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1c355acb4653","stem":"3. Low Birth Weight This is term used to describe babies born weighting less than 2500gm or 2,5kg , this is mostly caused by premature babies and intrauterine growth restriction where by the baby fail to grow due to problem from mother health, placental or baby condition.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e4bfb6be77fa","stem":"3.1. Epidemiology In 2013 nearly 22 million newborn – an estimate 16% of all babies born globally that year had low birth weight. Accurate monitoring is challenging, however, since nearly half of the infant of world’s infant are not weighted at birth in Ifakara the report of 2016 shows that 16 infant was born under weight, but South Africa has the highest incidence of low birth weight having 66%. Still a number of people in Kilombero district has tendency of ignoring clinical maternity. Just attending during complication phase. But some have excuses of being distant to SFRH incapable of enduring travel costs.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Epidemiological Measures","topicOriginal":"Epidemiological Measures","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Epidemiological Measures","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dd4d6ec872f1","stem":"3.1. Mild Anaemia Is a pathological condition arising as a result of low level of hemoglobin in the body. Anaemia can be classified as hemorrhagic, hemolytic, aplastic, nutritional anaemia. Most of children suffer from nutritional anaemia and show symptoms such as dizziness, fatigue, shortness of breath and headache.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5ca8a740ffd1","stem":"3.1.1. Epidemiology Mild anaemia is the worldwide disease affect most middle incoming countries such as Tanzania but in developing countries leading to maternal death and adverse pregnancy outcome despite of achievement of maternal and child health related programs still a problem. Tanzania is still a developing country, some regions and district are breathing but others are suffocating. Kilombero district like wise Ifakara town falls to the last group. Population is increasing and poverty same wise. Birth rate increases with low capability of handling such Angels. Thus unescapable of nutritional anaemia. It is how SFRH in 2016 demonstrates 14 patient were reported.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c845067fb450","stem":"5.1. Epidemiology Abortion is performed in whole world, and due to development of science and technology abortion can be done by using mifepristone medicine which was approved in US in 2000 and is used in 31 worldwide countries. In developing country like Tanzania abortion is the main cause of death in women below 60 years due to local method used in abortion. According to statistical data of SFRH 16 women performed abortion in 2016, same reasons explained in complications of birth accounts here.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-47b8bfc7d7b8","stem":"3.1. Mild Anaemia Mild anaemia is the worldwide disease affecting most low income countries such as Tanzania leading to maternal death and adverse pregnancy outcome despite of achievement of maternal and child health related programs, it is still a problem in Ifakara where 37children were admitted, 22 of them being male children and 15 being female children at SFRH in December 2016.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2234d49082e8","stem":"Prerenal azotemia, encountered with hypoperfusion of the kidneys, which decreases GFR as in shock states","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0ec11c6497a1","stem":"Renal, which is due to renal parenchymal damage","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Clinical Medicine","topic":"Renal and Urinary","topicOriginal":"Renal and Urinary","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Clinical Medicine","displayTopic":"Renal and Urinary","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOper